  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual portion of national road network receiving periodic maintenance</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2004-01-21" value="4.00" year="2004">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data is for Class 1 Network only in Upolu and Savai&apos;i.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2004-01-21"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="10.00"></target>
     <actual value="8.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Although the target missed its 10% end target, as much as 100 km of new Class 1 roads were added to the network since 2004.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Roads in good and fair condition as a share of total classified roads</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2004-01-21" value="75.00" year="2004">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator revised in the November 2013 restructuring.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2004-01-21"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="90.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The end target only refers to Upolu Island, which has a total of 747 km of roads.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="84.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data collected reflects Upolu Island roads only.  SIAM-2 was only implemented on Upolu.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Competitive price savings for maintenance works</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2004-01-21" value="0.00" year="2004">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2004-01-21"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="20.00"></target>
     <actual value="1.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2003, a couple of events occurred that significantly increased costs and reduced the value of this indicator. During thetransition of responsibility for road maintenance from MWTI to LTA, mowing and drainage clearing services were included as keymaintenance activities.  This increased the cost of maintenance by more than 40%.   After the 2009 tsunami, major rehabilitationand reconstruction works were included as part of maintenance activities in an effort to speed recovery, which included premiums torepair roads and bridges.  There was also a push to improve safety through the installation of speed humps and signage on majorroads, which increased costs.  Finally, the number of road zones that LTA was responsible for maintaining gradually increased from10 to 12 without a commensurate increase in budget.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal communities covered by CIM Plans</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2004-01-21" value="35.00" year="2004">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2004-01-21"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="100.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CIMs exercise provided a baseline of community infrastructure and its general condition.  Although anecdotal, the process ofpreparing the CIMS helped to educate villagers about the importance of keeping roadside drains cleared and possible hidden dangerswhen flooding occurs, all of which helped to lessen the impact of Tropical Cyclone Evan in December 2012.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="100.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
